  Release Notes for 0.5.0

 o FEATURE: "Cited most often by" on an author's page: who reads
            this person, as the mirror of who they work with. Names
            are clickable through to that author. Two OpenAlex calls
            and about two seconds, cached for a month

 o FEATURE: Volume, issue and pages are captured, stored, editable
            and exported. They were never collected before, so a
            178-entry BibTeX export carried not one of them despite
            146 entries having a DOI. Read from CrossRef, OpenAlex,
            or the PDF's own PRISM metadata

 o FEATURE: Citation (bibtex) key field in Edit metadata, with a
            Suggest button. A key is a human artefact — it often has
            to match one already in a group's .bib — and until now it
            could only be generated at export time

 o FEATURE: Import by PubMed or PMC identifier alongside DOI. Paste
            PMC5336473, a bare PubMed ID, or a URL from PubMed, PMC
            or Europe PMC

 o FEATURE: "Search using current metadata" in Edit metadata: search
            OpenAlex from the title, year and journal already in the
            dialog, rather than from a citation fragment you have to
            type out

 o FEATURE: The viewer's sidebar and the author page's people
            sections collapse, and remember whether you left them
            open

 o FEATURE: MCP: get_full_texts reads the publisher's JATS where we
            hold it, falling back to the PDF and then the abstract,
            and reports how much of the paper it returned so a
            summary can say what it actually read

 o CHANGE:  BibTeX-only entries show a drawn "no PDF" page rather
            than a stock icon that sat badly beside real thumbnails

 o CHANGE:  The author header puts the institution on its own line,
            with room to breathe

 o BUG-FIX: Alexandria no longer identifies its users as its author.
            An unconfigured copy sent the maintainer's email address
            to OpenAlex, CrossRef and Unpaywall, so every user's
            traffic was attributed to him. Set your own address in
            Preferences → Online services; without one, Unpaywall is
            skipped and the others fall back to the common pool

 o BUG-FIX: Typing in the search bar no longer runs a query and
            rebuilds every card per keystroke. Typing "coot" used to
            rebuild 331 cards; it now rebuilds five, once

 o BUG-FIX: BibTeX export no longer silently alters what it was
            given. A per-cent sign truncated its own field and
            everything after it — two abstracts lost two thirds of
            their text — page ranges were rewritten, and an "&" in a
            URL became a space

 o BUG-FIX: A .bib that uses one citation key twice keeps both
            papers. The second used to be dropped and its URL
            mangled; it is now re-parsed under a free key, and the
            rename is reported rather than done quietly

 o BUG-FIX: Corporate authors survive a round trip. "{{Meta
            Platforms, Inc.}}" was read as a personal name and
            written back as "Platforms, Inc. Meta"

 o BUG-FIX: An author's page showed the institution from whichever
            paper you opened them from — so a 2006 paper gave their
            2006 employer — while the sidebar showed the current one

 o BUG-FIX: The MCP server served one catalogue's records against
            another catalogue's file paths whenever the current
            catalogue was not the default. Nothing errored; the
            answers were simply about the wrong library

 o BUG-FIX: Importing a .bib no longer crashes on completion, so the
            progress bar comes down and the list refreshes

 o BUG-FIX: The JATS backfill no longer raises one notification per
            paper

